  "sourceInstructions": "<root xmlns=\"http://schemas.microsoft.com/sqlserver/2004/07/adventure-works/ProductModelManuInstructions\">AI-generated fictional demo instructions. Not validated engineering or safety instructions. Seat Tube (Product Number ST-9828) part sheet. Fictional part sheet for Seat Tube ST-9828, product 533, formed from its direct material and prepared for frame assembly.<Location LocationID=\"10\" SetupHours=\"0.1\" LaborHours=\"0.3\" MachineHours=\"0.2\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 10 - Frame Forming. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Frame Forming: conceptually form the supplied stock into the seat tube.<step>Set aside 1.00 EA of <material>Metal Bar 2 (Product Number MB-6061)</material> for one seat tube.</step><step>Using an <tool>assumed forming fixture</tool>, conceptually form the stock into a tube-shaped part; the actual forming method is unspecified. See illustration <diag>2005331</diag>.</step></Location><Location LocationID=\"30\" SetupHours=\"0.05\" LaborHours=\"0.2\" MachineHours=\"0.0\" LotSize=\"1\">Work Center 30 - Debur and Polish. Demo assumption: this part has no historical routing, so this existing work centre was assigned for demonstration only. Estimates are fictional demo assumptions. Debur and Polish: prepare and visually check the formed part.<step>Use an <tool>assumed deburring hand tool</tool> to remove apparent burrs from the formed part.</step><step>Visually check for obvious surface damage and remaining burrs; set aside any questionable part for review.</step></Location></root>",
